  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are playing many chess matches against Magnus. Every match is either a win or loss.\n\nUnsurprisingly, you are currently losing. The current score is A:BA:BA:B, where AAA is the number of matches you have won, and BBB is the number of matches Magnus has won.\n\nYou want to beat Magnus, i.e. win more matches than Magnus at the end. What is the minimum number of matches you still need to play to have any chance of being able to beat him?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe only line contains 222 integers - AAA and BBB, the current score.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the number of matches you still need to play.",
    "constraints": [
      "0≤A&lt;B≤50 \\le A \\lt B \\le 50≤A&lt;B≤5"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "0 1",
        "output": "2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nIf you play 222 more matches, it is possible that you win both and end up with a score of 2:12:12:1, and beat Magnus."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2 4",
        "output": "3",
        "explanation": ""
      }
    ]
  },
